# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. An export of a soft-deleted
# tree carries nothing, so the pass must be repeated after recovery; otherwise a
# delete behind the trim point is never applied.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceSoftDeleteSkipNotRetried
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a pass that ran while the source was soft-deleted is not retried, so its rows and reconcile are lost
PERTURBS: EndExport

--- FIND
               ELSE \/ topo # ex.topo0 \/ phys # ex.phys0 \/ ex.del0 \/ deleted \/ delDone # ex.dep0
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a soft delete does not leave the pass owed.
               ELSE \/ topo # ex.topo0 \/ phys # ex.phys0
--- END
